num_turns":5,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I'm rejecting this packet. The tests are good, but the packet's required records are missing.\n\n**What's good:**\n- The diff is one new test file, `tests/unit/docsCoServerHelpers.tests.js` (295 lines). It has the AGPL header and uses `@jest/globals` imports, and no production code changed. That fits the contract and the budget (1 of 2 files, 295 of 800 lines).\n- It mocks only infrastructure modules, and `tenantManager`/`utils` are spied on rather than changed. The test that checks the module loads fails outright if loading breaks, so the skipped helper tests can't hide that failure.\n- I checked `checkJwt`/`checkJwtHeader` against `DocsCoServer.js:1599-1639`. The assertions match today's behaviour: the result shape, the expired-token and invalid-token codes and description prefixes, how the default header, prefix and secret type are chosen, and returning null when the prefix doesn't match.\n- Edge cases are covered well:\n  - `getOpenFormatByEditor`: the string `'1'` and unknown or undefined editor types.\n  - `encryptPasswordParams`: a password of exactly the maximum length versus one character over.\n  - `getRequestParams`: a body that isn't valid JSON falls back to the query, and `tokenRequiredParams` drops the query values.\n\n**Weak assertions (minor):**\n- The \"missing secret\" test asserts `ctx.logger.warn` was called. That passes whether or not the empty-secret warning fires, because the verify-error path also calls `warn`. It should check for the `'empty secret'` message.\n- That test only asserts `res.code).not.toBeNull()` instead of the actual code.\n- The spies on `utils.encryptPassword` and `tenantManager.getTenantSecret` are never restored. That's harmless inside this file, but untidy.\n\n**Why I'm rejecting:**\n- The Executor log in the packet is empty. The packet requires the executor to record there what had to be mocked and why, as input for the core reassessment. The contract also says surprising behaviour must be recorded in the packet. Examples:\n  - The string `'1'` maps to the Word format.\n  - `operationContext` and `tenantManager` require each other and only load in one order.\n  - `tenantManager` can't be mocked with `jest.mock`.\n  - A missing secret only logs a warning and still tries to verify the token.\n- AGENTS.md says these records must live in the repository, not just in code comments. Lessons for the Atlas and the friction entry are missing too.\n\nVERDICT: REJECT Fill the packet's Executor log (mocked modules and why, the operationContext/tenantManager circular require, surprising behaviours such as the string '1' giving the Word format and a missing secret only logging a warning) plus Lessons for the Atlas and friction; ideally also assert the 'empty secret' warn message and the exact error code in the missing-secret test.","ttft_ms":7451,"type":"result","duration_ms":32717,"uuid":"b0f3fed9-8d11-45c7-9703-870aa7f28b17","ttft_stream_ms":5801,"time_to_request_ms":288,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":6,"system_prompt":166,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":3,"input_attachments":20,"input_hooks":2,"conversation_append":1,"transcript_persist":11,"tool_pool_refresh":0,"init_message":6,"init_frame_send":3,"engine_pickup":1,"loop_entry":3,"message_prep":1,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":2,"request_announcements":14,"query_setup":3,"auto_mode_context_wait":7,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":25,"message_normalization":3,"client_creation":2,"request_build":8},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":32,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":158,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"process_rss_mib_turn_start":215,"process_anon_mib_turn_start":139,"process_rss_mib_result":221,"process_anon_mib_result":132,"process_peak_rss_mib":253,"process_cpu_ms_turn":1152,"process_wall_ms_turn":32716,"process_cpu_ms_streaming":316,"process_wall_ms_streaming":18784,"main_stream_count":5,"main_stream_event_cou